            "location": "src/workflow/code-review/investigation/continuation-types.ts:50-52",
            "message": "The LLD's dataModelChanges schemaDiff for InvestigationBackend pins the qualification fields `pinnedReads`, `readOnly` and `cancellable` to the literal type `true` (a compile-time guarantee that only qualified backends can satisfy the interface). The implemented InvestigationBackend.qualification types these fields as plain `boolean`, which lets a backend object type-check with `false` values. Runtime guards in continuation-policy.ts's assertInvestigationBindings (`if(!q.pinnedReads||!q.readOnly||!q.cancellable...)`) still reject such a backend before dispatch, so no incorrect behavior results, but the static type no longer matches the approved schemaDiff's literal-`true` contract.",
            "expectationRef": "LLD dataModelChanges[0].schemaDiff (InvestigationBackend.qualification: pinnedReads/readOnly/cancellable typed as literal `true`)"
          }
        ]
